      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In this report the Authors describe the case of a 3-years-old boy with a septate gallbladder and chronic abdominal pain: an uncommon clinical condition at this age. Diagnosis was confirmed by ultrasound scan and oral cholecistogram. As congenital gallbladder abnormalities may cause, although rarely, chronic abdominal pain, also in the first years of the life, they must be included in the differential diagnosis."},
